  "label": "Misogyny",
  "description": "The meme's use of vulgar, sexually explicit language in a context involving women (who appear to be public figures or activists) can be interpreted as reinforcing misogynistic tropes. Misogyny involves the hatred, prejudice, or discrimination against women, often manifesting as the assumption that women are sexually available or that their public roles are somehow diminished by sexualized commentary. The juxtaposition of serious, formal media appearances with crude sexual innuendo can be seen as a form of objectification and devaluation of women's public personas.",
